  "title": "Numbers",
  "summary": "Count from zero to sixty-nine, say how old you are and ask how much something costs. Numbers are everywhere: prices, ages and shopping.",
  "canDo": [
    "Count from zero to twenty, including the tricky 17, 18 and 19.",
    "Count in tens and units from twenty-one to sixty-nine.",
    "Say how old I am, using j'ai … ans.",
    "Ask how much something costs, and say a price in euros."
  ],
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "u05-l1",
      "title": "Zero to ten",
      "goal": "Count from zero to ten and say how many things there are.",
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": "u05-l1-n1",
          "title": "The numbers 0 to 10",
          "body": "Learn each number as a word, like any other word. **un** is *one*, but it is also *a* before a masculine noun: *un stylo*. Count up or down by saying the numbers in a row, with a comma between them.",
          "examples": [
            {
              "fr": "Un, deux, trois !",
              "en": "One, two, three!"
            },
            {
              "fr": "Zéro, un, deux.",
              "en": "Zero, one, two."
            },
            {
              "fr": "Dix, neuf, huit !",
              "en": "Ten, nine, eight!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "u05-l1-n2",
          "title": "Plural nouns after numbers",
          "body": "After **deux** and any bigger number, the noun is **plural**: *deux stylos*, *six chaises*. Only **un** goes with a singular noun. **Deux** and **six** end with a letter that is silent, but before a word that starts with a vowel it is said like *z*: *deux étudiants* is said *deuz-étudiants*.",
          "examples": [
            {
              "fr": "Deux stylos, madame.",
              "en": "Two pens, madam."
            },
            {
              "fr": "Deux étudiants, monsieur.",
              "en": "Two students, sir."
            },
            {
              "fr": "Quatre stylos et cinq livres.",
              "en": "Four pens and five books."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "words": [
